WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:35.330
<b>Future Island, Egghead</b>

3
00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:42.420
Seems I've climbed aboard a ship
with a storm for a captain. What luck I have.

4
00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.750
You certainly are a handful,
aren't you, Luffy?

5
00:01:47.170 --> 00:01:48.250
Luffy!

6
00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:51.510
Your dream is great! I love it!

7
00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:52.590
Oh, yeah?

8
00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.470
I'm so happy!

9
00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.140
Oh, hey! Easy there, buddy!

10
00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.560
Crazy, but it's just
perfect for you.

11
00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.190
No way that's gonna happen until
you're King of the Pirates, though!

12
00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.880
Better get cracking. One more Road
Poneglyph to Laugh Tale!

13
00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:08.200
We're in the homestretch,
everybody!

14
00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:10.960
Perhaps so, but it won't
be an easy stretch.

15
00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.250
We have a dangerous
journey ahead.

16
00:02:13.330 --> 00:02:17.150
The last Road Poneglyph, will be
the most difficult one to find.

17
00:02:19.190 --> 00:02:22.950
Not to mention, we don't have
a single lead to follow up on.

18
00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:28.120
Unlike the others, no one has
been able to find this Poneglyph.

19
00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:31.660
We're sailing straight
into uncharted waters.

20
00:02:40.970 --> 00:02:42.810
<b>Marine Headquarters
New World</b>

21
00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:46.340
It's Flame Emperor Sabo!

22
00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:48.220
He's calling the Kamabakka
Queendom!

23
00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.090
Good!

24
00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:50.570
We'll hunt him down.

25
00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.410
Let's trace that call, men!

26
00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:54.010
The signal's
not being jammed.

27
00:02:54.090 --> 00:02:54.880
That's strange.

28
00:02:54.960 --> 00:02:57.770
Why isn't he using a white
transponder snail to keep us out?

29
00:02:57.770 --> 00:02:59.810
It must be an emergency call.

30
00:02:59.890 --> 00:03:01.290
We better make this quick!

31
00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:04.140
We need to get his location
before he hangs up!

32
00:03:04.480 --> 00:03:06.270
We can't let this leak go!

33
00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:10.250
<b>Room of Authority
Pangaea Castle
The Holy Land, Mary Geoise</b>

34
00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:16.590
The trace was successful!

35
00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:17.670
Where is it from?

36
00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:20.050
The kingdom of Lulusia.

37
00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.480
From Lulusia.

38
00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:25.260
Well, well.

39
00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:29.200
We've been informed that the insurgents
in Lulusia successfully overthrew

40
00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:32.380
the country's monarchy at the start
of the Eight Nation Revolution.

41
00:03:32.380 --> 00:03:34.880
It's the perfect place
for Sabo to hide.

42
00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:37.160
Then it's settled.

43
00:03:37.240 --> 00:03:39.240
Sabo's quite
the unlucky fellow.

44
00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.000
It's not luck.

45
00:03:44.130 --> 00:03:45.950
This is his destiny.

46
00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:51.590
<b>Kamabakka Queendom</b>

47
00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:52.480
I'm fine.

48
00:03:52.560 --> 00:03:54.000
Just glad I got through.

49
00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:54.880
Oh!

50
00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.120
I'm glad too!

51
00:03:57.490 --> 00:03:58.440
Yeah, me too!

52
00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:00.880
But you sure took
your sweet time calling.

53
00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:02.440
What was the big hold-up?

54
00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:03.030
Darling!

55
00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:04.400
I've been worried
sick about you!

56
00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:06.180
How could you do
this to your dear friend?

57
00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.420
I'm sorry, everyone!

58
00:04:08.980 --> 00:04:10.980
You stop the possessing
right now!

59
00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:09.870
You stop that!

60
00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.020
We love you!

61
00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.880
I have a feeling it's a bit
too early to celebrate.

62
00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:17.810
You didn't call just to let us
know you're alive, did you?

63
00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.160
So, what's the lowdown?

64
00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.810
For starters, you read
the article, right?

65
00:04:23.890 --> 00:04:26.420
So you probably have
some questions for me.

66
00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:27.710
