<b>REVOLUTIONARY ARMY CHIEF OF STAFF SABO

ASSASSINATES KING COBRA OF ARABASTA</b>

67
00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:37.980
Dragon, it's true that
King Cobra is dead.

68
00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:44.910
I didn't kill him.

69
00:04:47.010 --> 00:04:49.470
I knew it! We never
doubted you, Sabo!

70
00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:57.230
We always believed in you,
my innocent little lamb!

71
00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:58.070
Before I fled from Mary Geoise,
I saw something I still can't believe.

72
00:04:58.070 --> 00:05:02.810
What did you see, Sabo?

73
00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.580
<b>Kingdom of Lulusia
Grand Line</b>

74
00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:22.870
Good idea.

75
00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:23.310
...What to do?

76
00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:32.840
What's going on?

77
00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:34.480
Never seen clouds like that.

78
00:05:34.560 --> 00:05:36.310
No, that isn't a cloud.

79
00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.010
There's something
floating up there.

80
00:05:41.790 --> 00:05:43.970
You insects won't pay
for this treachery!

81
00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:45.950
You think the navy
won't hear of this?

82
00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:48.410
<b>Princess Comane
Kingdom of Lulusia King Seki
Kingdom of Lulusia</b>

83
00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.950
They'll burn you at the stake
and impale what's left of you!

84
00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.910
Father, let me scold
the traitors too!

85
00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:53.510
Prepare to be
eradicated, vermin!

86
00:05:53.590 --> 00:05:56.090
Lord Seki, please just listen!

87
00:05:56.170 --> 00:05:58.960
This revolt has been a long
time coming, can't you see?

88
00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:02.240
This wouldn't have happened if you
had thought of your people's welfare!

89
00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:03.040
What?!

90
00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:07.190
Why should a king waste his time thinking
about a bunch of lowly peasants?

91
00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:09.920
Know your place,
you insolent worms!

92
00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:11.970
All we want is for you
to admit your wrongs!

93
00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:15.330
Please, my lord, we won't
hurt you, I swear, just a little!

94
00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:19.370
Get me out of this cage, now!

95
00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:38.600
I was still at the reverie
at the time, in Pangaea Castle.

96
00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.570
And I saw the Empty Throne...

97
00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:43.750
Communications, cut off
your transponder, snail.

98
00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:44.710
Huh?

99
00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.680
Do I need to repeat myself?

100
00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:48.640
Sorry, sir!

101
00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:52.370
They always say that
there's no king of the world!

102
00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.460
So no one is
supposed to sit there!

103
00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:59.720
Communications,
listen carefully.

104
00:07:09.070 --> 00:07:13.230
You did not trace any calls
today, do you understand?

105
00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:17.040
Yeah, but I'm scared!

106
00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:24.700
You didn't overhear
a single word.

107
00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:29.660
And as for Lulusia...

108
00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:38.450
I've never heard of it.

109
00:07:47.020 --> 00:07:49.510
In fact, it never existed.

110
00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:11.630
What's happening now?

111
00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:36.660
Sabo?

112
00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:38.400
Are you there?

113
00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:49.830
A major seaquake just hit
up the southeast coast!

114
00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:51.480
Make emergency
preparations!

115
00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:53.060
A tsunami is coming!

116
00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:04.320
<b>A Few Days Later</b>

117
00:09:10.490 --> 00:09:12.150
We're all gonna die!

118
00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:22.130
It's freezing!

119
00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.510
This is a nightmare!

120
00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:26.290
Please don't kill me again!

121
00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:27.450
We talked about this!

122
00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:34.780
There's a Sea King too!

123
00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:36.310
Hahaha!

124
00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.960
What kind of madness is this?

125
00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:52.490
Hey, aren't you cold
without a shirt on?

126
00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:53.260
I'm fine.

127
00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:55.130
Feeling hot or cold
is all in your head.

128
00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:56.230
Oh, I see.

129
00:09:56.310 --> 00:09:59.150
So your head's well insulated
because it's full of moss.

130
00:09:59.230 --> 00:10:00.180
What's that?

131
00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:01.700
You think you're cold?

132
00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.050
Wait till I throw
you in the ocean!

133
00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:04.210
Let's see you try!

134
00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:07.180
Could you two possibly pick
a worse time to argue?!

135
00:10:07.260 --> 00:10:08.060
Jinbe!

136
00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:10.050
Watch out for icebergs!

137
00:10:10.620 --> 00:10:11.420
Roger!

138
00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.490
Furl the sails quickly!

139
00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:27.590
The winds are far too strong!

140
00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:28.970
You heard the man!

141
00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:29.850
Let's go!

142
00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:39.290
Strong Right!

143
00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:37.520
Strong right!

144
00:10:47.790 --> 00:10:49.380
Take up the pace, moss head!

145
00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:50.470
You're holding me back!

146
00:10:50.470 --> 00:10:56.630
You really like the sound
of your own voice, don't you?

147
00:10:56.710 --> 00:10:58.010
Nami, do you see any land?

148
00:10:58.060 --> 00:10:59.460
No, not yet.

149
00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:01.850
But we should come
up on an island soon.

150
00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:06.130
With this snow, I'm assuming we're
probably within range of a winter island.

151
00:11:06.210 --> 00:11:09.270
And it must be one
with an especially harsh climate.

152
00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.960
Seems like they're
having a hard time.

153
00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:18.100
I better go help.

154
00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:19.470
How cute!

155
00:11:19.550 --> 00:11:20.590
I love the hat.

156
00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:21.370
Looking good.

157
00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:27.730
With this woven headpiece that Otama
bestowed upon me, the falling snow

158
00:11:27.810 --> 00:11:28.910
shall prove no peril.

159
00:11:28.990 --> 00:11:29.790
Huh?

160
00:11:34.870 --> 00:11:36.460
Hey, Nami!

161
00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:37.830
Come check this out!

162
00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:38.710
Yeah?

163
00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:41.320
What?

164
00:11:47.210 --> 00:11:50.350
What is that thing?

165
00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:53.660
Looks like a warm eddy
of considerable size!

166
00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:54.370
No way!

167
00:11:54.370 --> 00:11:55.390
That's an eddy?

168
00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:56.630
Oh great!

169
00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:57.660
What now?

170
00:11:58.230 --> 00:11:59.130
That thing's huge!

171
00:11:59.130 --> 00:12:01.010
How is an eddy
floating in the air?

172
00:12:01.090 --> 00:12:03.880
It's concentrated heat!

173
00:12:03.960 --> 00:12:07.140
It must have warmed up so
much that it rose above the sea!

174
00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:09.060
There's no way that's right!

175
00:12:10.930 --> 00:12:13.000
Like a big, beautiful afro.

176
00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:14.530
Get away, Jinbe!

177
00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:15.610
It'll suck us in!

178
00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:16.850
Leave it to me!

179
00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:18.070
Wait!

180
00:12:19.360 --> 00:12:22.130
There's someone floating
up there in the water!

181
00:12:23.140 --> 00:12:23.810
Oh, what?

182
00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:25.370
You think there's a mermaid?

183
00:12:25.450 --> 00:12:26.750
Oh, what's that?

184
00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.840
I think Luffy's right.

185
00:12:35.920 --> 00:12:37.720
I heard a little girl crying out.

186
00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:38.540
You heard that?

187
00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:39.430
From underwater?

188
00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.760
What the hell's going on?

189
00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:51.610
Even if there is someone,
what can we do?

190
00:12:53.560 --> 00:12:55.150
I'll just cut him out.

191
00:13:00.140 --> 00:13:05.000
If you put so much as a scratch on that
girl, I swear I'm gonna fillet your ass!

192
00:13:05.080 --> 00:13:06.350
Like I would miss!

193
00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:18.560
Here we go.

194
00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:28.110
One sword style...

195
00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:30.010
Bird dance!

196
00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:35.910
He cut it!

197
00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:41.680
Greetings, comrades!

198
00:13:42.140 --> 00:13:42.970
I heard a fuss!

199
00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:43.780
What ails thee?

200
00:13:43.780 --> 00:13:44.620
Worry not!

201
00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.340
Woven-Hat Chopperemon
is here to...

202
00:13:49.620 --> 00:13:50.870
...the wind's too strong!

203
00:13:50.900 --> 00:13:52.820
Why didn't you stay inside?

204
00:13:52.900 --> 00:13:53.750
You had it all...

205
00:13:53.770 --> 00:13:55.420
...and you threw it all away!

206
00:13:55.900 --> 00:13:57.650
Somebody help me!

207
00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:00.220
Hold on!

208
00:14:03.260 --> 00:14:04.160
Thanks, Luffy!

209
00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.510
Give me a break!

210
00:14:08.590 --> 00:14:09.480
Not you two!

211
00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:11.280
What the hell are they doing?

212
00:14:11.360 --> 00:14:12.160
Come on!

213
00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:26.680
<b>Jewelry Bonney "the Glutton"
Worst Generation</b>
<b>Bounty: 320 Million</b>

214
00:14:26.730 --> 00:14:28.630
There's a little kid up there!

215
00:14:29.390 --> 00:14:30.290
Who is that?

216
00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:31.550
Huh?

217
00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:36.170
Huh?

218
00:14:39.010 --> 00:14:39.890
Who's there?

219
00:14:41.930 --> 00:14:42.850
Thank you!

220
00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:44.990
Where's the monster?

221
00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:47.450
She's okay!

222
00:14:48.110 --> 00:14:49.120
That's a relief!

223
00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:49.510
But, uh...

224
00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:52.290
They're kinda just floatin'
up there, aren't they?

225
00:14:53.480 --> 00:14:54.310
Hold up!

226
00:14:54.390 --> 00:14:55.800
She's yellin' something!

227
00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:59.500
Look down!

228
00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:02.120
She said look down!

229
00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:11.570
What is that thing?

230
00:15:11.650 --> 00:15:12.730
Go away!

231
00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:16.450
– Oh my gosh! Oh my gosh! Oh my gosh!
– What's going on?!

232
00:15:16.450 --> 00:15:17.370
Someone help!

233
00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:22.170
We need to get
out of here now!

234
00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:23.860
Sail away!

235
00:15:38.320 --> 00:15:42.260
Is this how it ends for us?

236
00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:43.860
Jinbe!

237
00:15:42.820 --> 00:15:43.620
Hurry!

238
00:15:44.430 --> 00:15:45.500
Come on, Jinbe!

239
00:15:45.580 --> 00:15:46.500
Step on it!

240
00:15:46.580 --> 00:15:47.610
Let's go!

241
00:15:48.160 --> 00:15:50.080
You can leave it to me!

242
00:15:50.160 --> 00:15:51.180
Move it!

243
00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:02.460
What the hell is that thing?

244
00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:05.320
I thought it was a shark,
but it's way too big!

245
00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.590
And it looks like
it's made of metal!

246
00:16:10.230 --> 00:16:11.470
Hold on tight!

247
00:16:11.550 --> 00:16:13.620
We're about to hit the water!

248
00:16:20.890 --> 00:16:21.950
This isn't good!

249
00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:24.160
They fell straight into the sea!

250
00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:25.400
I need to go now!

251
00:16:26.070 --> 00:16:26.890
Franky!

252
00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:28.640
Take the helm for me!

253
00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:30.930
I'm going after them!

254
00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.450
Bring the ship around to us!

255
00:16:34.560 --> 00:16:35.500
No problem!

256
00:16:35.580 --> 00:16:36.980
I got your back, bro!

257
00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:48.970
I said no problem,
but these waters are rough!

258
00:16:49.050 --> 00:16:50.010
I can't find them!

259
00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:52.910
Well, I got some
tricks up my sleeve!

260
00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:02.200
Ship's bottom!

261
00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:08.490
Rapid screw!

262
00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:13.270
Hop to it, baby!

263
00:17:14.300 --> 00:17:18.430
<b>SHIP'S BOTTOM:</b>
<b>RABBIT SCREW</b>

264
00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:21.740
Alright!

265
00:17:22.240 --> 00:17:23.690
Franky's coming
for you, bros!

266
00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:24.800
Don't you worry!

267
00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:38.920
Luffy!

268
00:17:39.410 --> 00:17:40.240
Chopper!

269
00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:41.660
Stupid snow!

270
00:17:41.740 --> 00:17:42.540
I can't see!

271
00:17:47.440 --> 00:17:48.260
Franky!

272
00:17:52.020 --> 00:17:52.270
Move!

273
00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:54.200
We got torpedoes!

274
00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:54.980
No!

275
00:17:57.060 --> 00:17:57.860
Water!

276
00:18:00.360 --> 00:18:01.060
Women!

277
00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:01.800
Luffy!

278
00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:04.460
Oh crap!

279
00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.160
It's gonna capsize!

280
00:18:07.500 --> 00:18:08.300
No!

281
00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:09.980
No!

282
00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:27.480
It sounded like there was
an explosion up above!

283
00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:31.670
Chopper!

284
00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:32.370
Luffy!

285
00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:34.060
I'm almost there!

286
00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.870
You're going to be all right!

287
00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:44.950
We're nearly to the surface!

288
00:18:45.030 --> 00:18:46.210
You'll be safe soon!

289
00:18:46.620 --> 00:18:48.330
I won't let you die!

290
00:18:54.750 --> 00:18:56.510
This current is far too strong!

291
00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:58.750
The Sunny can't
navigate through this!

292
00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:01.750
Thanks, Jinbe!

293
00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:03.100
You saved us!

294
00:19:03.180 --> 00:19:05.470
Well, there's no need
to worry anymore.

295
00:19:08.650 --> 00:19:11.650
Now we just have to find
our way back to the Sunny.

296
00:19:15.850 --> 00:19:18.010
Hmm?

297
00:19:23.570 --> 00:19:24.370
Hmm?

298
00:19:27.030 --> 00:19:28.710
Something wrong, Gp?

299
00:19:30.130 --> 00:19:31.450
Hold on tight!

300
00:19:34.930 --> 00:19:36.640
We'll head for the sea floor!

301
00:19:37.230 --> 00:19:39.200
Everyone take a deep
breath while you can!

302
00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:40.330
We're going under!

303
00:19:47.430 --> 00:19:48.360
Here we go!

304
00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:08.440
Huh?

305
00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:11.030
Dammit!

306
00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:12.920
The current's way too fast!

307
00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:14.330
We can't surface!

308
00:20:15.120 --> 00:20:16.410
We're all gonna drown!

309
00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:18.310
Why am I into water?

310
00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:20.140
What the hell's going on?!

311
00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:22.240
Hang in there, Robin!

312
00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:24.980
Nami!

313
00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:18.950
This ain't good!

314
00:21:19.300 --> 00:21:21.480
We gotta come up
with something fast!

315
00:21:22.720 --> 00:21:24.510
We're all dead!

316
00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:26.050
Hi,

317
00:21:39.030 --> 00:21:41.740
<b>At a Nearby Island</b>
<b>Marine Branch G-14</b>

318
00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:40.850
Everyone!

319
00:21:40.930 --> 00:21:41.750
I'm back!

320
00:21:41.740 --> 00:21:45.200
<b>Captain Tashigi
Marine Headquarters</b>

321
00:21:42.410 --> 00:21:44.290
Are you ready
for your medicine?

322
00:21:45.830 --> 00:21:47.120
One cup each!

323
00:21:47.200 --> 00:21:48.240
Drink it up!

324
00:21:50.230 --> 00:21:51.270
Okay, fine!

325
00:21:51.650 --> 00:21:52.570
I'm gonna drink it!

326
00:21:52.570 --> 00:21:54.090
But only for you, Tashigi!

327
00:21:54.930 --> 00:21:56.190
That's a good boy!

328
00:21:56.270 --> 00:21:58.970
Sorry, guys, but you'll have
to drink every last drop!

329
00:21:58.930 --> 00:22:00.270
This tastes weird!

330
00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:01.170
It's gross!

331
00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:02.050
I hate it!

332
00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:03.400
Be brave!

333
00:22:03.480 --> 00:22:04.360
You can do it!

334
00:22:04.440 --> 00:22:08.200
Do I really gotta drink
the whole glass?

335
00:22:08.280 --> 00:22:08.970
Yeah!

336
00:22:08.970 --> 00:22:11.250
Then you'll turn back
to your normal size!

337
00:22:11.330 --> 00:22:12.050
Alright!

338
00:22:12.130 --> 00:22:14.600
If you say it'll fix me,
then I'll drink too!

339
00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:15.840
Tashigi!

340
00:22:16.350 --> 00:22:17.230
What do you think?

341
00:22:17.230 --> 00:22:18.250
Do I look smaller?

342
00:22:18.330 --> 00:22:19.030
Mm-hmm!

343
00:22:19.480 --> 00:22:20.720
You look great, Mocha!

344
00:22:20.800 --> 00:22:21.750
It's working!

345
00:22:21.830 --> 00:22:24.090
Does that mean I
can go home soon?

346
00:22:24.170 --> 00:22:24.980
Uh-huh!

347
00:22:25.060 --> 00:22:26.640
Just keep up the good work!

348
00:22:26.720 --> 00:22:27.960
You're almost there!

349
00:22:28.040 --> 00:22:29.120
Tashigi!

350
00:22:30.730 --> 00:22:31.960
Vice Admiral Doll!

351
00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:34.180
Can I borrow you for a sec?

352
00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:41.460
<b>Vice Admiral Doll
Marine Branch G-14 Commander</b>

353
00:22:37.450 --> 00:22:39.520
Helmeppo is driving
everyone crazy.

354
00:22:39.600 --> 00:22:41.810
Come on, can you
please talk to him?

355
00:22:41.890 --> 00:22:44.530
Look, I'm sorry,
but I can't help you.

356
00:22:44.910 --> 00:22:47.890
He has every right to be
worried about his friend.

357
00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:49.150
And I see why.

358
00:22:49.230 --> 00:22:51.760
We all wish we could do
something for Koby.

359
00:22:52.250 --> 00:22:54.110
Do something for Koby!

360
00:22:54.650 --> 00:22:58.030
He's our brother in arms,
but we can't let him die!

361
00:22:57.180 --> 00:23:00.720
Both of us are
on our knees begging you!

362
00:22:58.520 --> 00:23:04.700
<b>Commander Hibari
Marine Headquarters
(SWORD) Lieutenant Commander Helmeppo
Marine Headquarters
(SWORD)</b>

363
00:23:00.800 --> 00:23:02.900
Koby has been
so good to me!

364
00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:04.840
He deserves better than this!

365
00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:07.950
<b>Rear Admiral Prince Grus
Marine Headquarters
(SWORD)</b>

366
00:23:04.920 --> 00:23:07.880
We have to go to Pirate
Island before it's too late!

367
00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:08.940
Please, Prince!

368
00:23:11.570 --> 00:23:14.930
If you won't help us, we'll
have to go by ourselves!

369
00:23:17.960 --> 00:23:19.880
Please, have a heart!

370
00:23:20.990 --> 00:23:25.260
I'm sorry, but I won't move an inch
until you promise to help us!

371
00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:29.690
You really expect to waltz into
Blackbeard's turf and come back alive?

372
00:23:29.770 --> 00:23:31.020
You'd be picking a fight.

373
00:23:31.060 --> 00:23:32.310
A fight with an Emperor.

374
00:23:32.960 --> 00:23:36.590
This place is a death trap.

375
00:23:36.670 --> 00:23:40.020
You poke the hive,
and you're gonna get swarmed.

376
00:23:40.540 --> 00:23:44.340
A whole horde of bloodthirsty
pirates will shoot you up.

377
00:23:47.860 --> 00:23:50.040
That's why they
call it Full of Lead.

378
00:23:51.110 --> 00:23:53.520
Egghead's pretty close
to here, you know.

379
00:23:55.330 --> 00:23:57.180
We can take
the seraphim, too!

380
00:23:57.790 --> 00:23:59.370
You've lost your mind!

381
00:23:59.450 --> 00:24:01.070
No way in hell, okay?

382
00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:03.230
Let's all just calm down.

383
00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:08.990
I wish we could contact
Drake with that shot, too.

384
00:24:10.270 --> 00:24:11.890
There's nothing we can do!

385
00:24:17.120 --> 00:24:18.180
Try to understand.

386
00:24:20.560 --> 00:24:23.020
Koby!

387
00:24:27.880 --> 00:24:28.900
What?

388
00:24:28.780 --> 00:24:31.490
<b>Luffy's Group</b>

389
00:24:28.980 --> 00:24:31.460
You seriously don't
know who I am?

390
00:24:31.920 --> 00:24:33.300
Nope, no clue.

391
00:24:33.380 --> 00:24:36.290
We're both part of the worst
generation, stupid!

392
00:24:36.370 --> 00:24:37.560
Did you just forget me?

393
00:24:37.640 --> 00:24:38.930
Or everyone else, too?

394
00:24:39.380 --> 00:24:41.200
Oh cool, you're
the worst, too, huh?

395
00:24:41.280 --> 00:24:41.980
Nice!

396
00:24:42.460 --> 00:24:44.530
Don't say it like
that, you idiot.

397
00:24:46.980 --> 00:24:49.260
I was there at Sabaody,
too, you know.

398
00:24:49.340 --> 00:24:50.480
Two years back.

399
00:24:51.660 --> 00:24:53.210
The name is Bonney.

400
00:24:53.630 --> 00:24:54.610
We're rivals.

401
00:24:54.690 --> 00:24:55.510
You got that?

402
00:24:56.590 --> 00:24:59.070
That aside, you
still saved my life.

403
00:25:00.220 --> 00:25:01.340
So thanks for that.

404
00:25:02.190 --> 00:25:04.290
Aw, hey, don't
mention it, boggy.

405
00:25:04.370 --> 00:25:05.770
Bonney, dammit!

406
00:25:05.850 --> 00:25:07.390
Cut that out, Luffy!

407
00:25:10.710 --> 00:25:11.670
Stop it!

408
00:25:11.750 --> 00:25:12.570
It's cold!

409
00:25:13.630 --> 00:25:16.130
Now I'm immune
to your wicked waterways!

410
00:25:16.770 --> 00:25:18.830
Well, I'm immune
to your immunity!

411
00:25:18.910 --> 00:25:19.610
What!

412
00:25:20.670 --> 00:25:22.020
This guy is an Emperor?

413
00:25:25.940 --> 00:25:29.080
By the way, why is
your wanted poster so weird?

414
00:25:29.160 --> 00:25:31.200
I thought your hair
turned white.

415
00:25:31.280 --> 00:25:33.490
The newspapers made
a big deal out of it.

416
00:25:33.570 --> 00:25:34.300
Oh yeah?

417
00:25:34.380 --> 00:25:35.280
That's funny.

418
00:25:37.860 --> 00:25:40.540
That's just how I look
when I'm totally free!

419
00:25:40.620 --> 00:25:42.110
Oh, forget I asked.

420
00:25:42.190 --> 00:25:43.840
So what happened
to your friends?

421
00:25:43.840 --> 00:25:44.960
Think they're okay?

422
00:25:45.930 --> 00:25:48.310
I'm sure they're fine.

423
00:25:50.060 --> 00:25:51.520
And what about your crew?

424
00:25:51.600 --> 00:25:53.950
I didn't see your ship
out there either.

425
00:25:55.450 --> 00:25:57.120
I came here alone.

426
00:25:58.090 --> 00:26:01.570
As for my ship, it got gobbled
up by that giant monster.

427
00:26:01.650 --> 00:26:03.640
Stupid metal bastard!

428
00:26:03.720 --> 00:26:05.060
I'm sorry to hear it.

429
00:26:06.080 --> 00:26:09.030
Man, I really gotta
find me some grub.

430
00:26:11.830 --> 00:26:13.360
Actually, I'm hungry too.

431
00:26:13.850 --> 00:26:15.920
No good place to eat.

432
00:26:16.000 --> 00:26:17.260
Good idea!

433
00:26:17.340 --> 00:26:20.310
Let's find some money
and head to a restaurant.

434
00:26:20.390 --> 00:26:21.120
What?

435
00:26:21.200 --> 00:26:22.570
Are you guys stupid?

436
00:26:22.650 --> 00:26:24.300
There's no restaurants here!

437
00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:25.460
Huh?

438
00:26:26.830 --> 00:26:29.210
This island belongs
to the government!

439
00:26:31.440 --> 00:26:32.910
Let me fill you in.

440
00:26:33.300 --> 00:26:36.020
They call this place
Egghead Island.

441
00:26:36.100 --> 00:26:40.690
Dr. Vegapunk's lab is here, and thanks
to his inventions, they say this island is

442
00:26:40.770 --> 00:26:42.860
500 years in the future.

443
00:26:44.130 --> 00:26:45.640
Dr. Vegapunk?

444
00:26:45.720 --> 00:26:47.370
I've heard that name before!

445
00:26:50.420 --> 00:26:53.020
I'm here to give him
a piece of my mind.

446
00:26:53.100 --> 00:26:54.490
We've got business.

447
00:27:10.650 --> 00:27:11.500
Is everyone here?

448
00:27:11.550 --> 00:27:12.610
Are you all right?

449
00:27:15.390 --> 00:27:19.490
Did the Sunny
survive all that?

450
00:27:27.590 --> 00:27:28.950
It's... it's...

451
00:27:29.550 --> 00:27:30.760
a giant robot!

452
00:27:32.850 --> 00:27:34.510
But who is operating it?

453
00:27:47.420 --> 00:27:48.310
Careful!

454
00:27:48.390 --> 00:27:49.380
Here they come!

455
00:27:50.380 --> 00:27:51.730
That was a bust.

456
00:27:52.570 --> 00:27:55.260
Just... where did I
go wrong this time?

457
00:27:56.980 --> 00:28:00.220
Guess I can't code the instincts
out of a living thing.

458
00:28:02.340 --> 00:28:04.040
Whatever, I'll work on that.

459
00:28:04.120 --> 00:28:06.120
I don't know who
you are, but thanks!

460
00:28:06.200 --> 00:28:07.740
You saved our asses!

461
00:28:07.820 --> 00:28:08.960
I owe you one!

462
00:28:09.410 --> 00:28:10.480
Hardly.

463
00:28:10.560 --> 00:28:13.210
I'm just here to troubleshoot
my mecha shark.

464
00:28:18.020 --> 00:28:22.490
All I ordered that hunk of junk to do was
scout, report, and bombard, not eat

465
00:28:22.570 --> 00:28:25.230
the target and destroy all
their freaking valuables.

466
00:28:26.060 --> 00:28:27.710
Must be a programming error.

467
00:28:36.420 --> 00:28:37.220
What?

468
00:28:37.730 --> 00:28:41.080
You filthy pirates really
thought I came to save you?

469
00:28:41.160 --> 00:28:45.830
A genius government scientist like me
has no business with the likes of you!

470
00:28:49.430 --> 00:28:51.890
My name is Dr. Vegapunk!

471
00:28:54.170 --> 00:28:54.970
What?
